{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry the orders@ mailbox has gone missing from Outlook. Here are a few things to try:\n\n1. Close Outlook completely and open it again. Shared mailboxes usually reappear on their own after a restart.\n2. If it's still missing, add it yourself: go to File > Account Settings > Account Settings, double-click your account, then More Settings > Advanced tab > Add, and type orders@.\n3. Check whether you can open it in Outlook on the web: right-click your folder list, choose 'Add shared folder or mailbox', and enter orders@.\n\nPlease reply and let us know: (a) whether either step brings the mailbox back, and (b) whether Outlook on the web lets you open orders@ or says you don't have permission. If you don't have permission, someone may have removed your access. In that case we'll pass it to our Tier 2 team, and they'll need the mailbox owner to approve giving it back.",
  "internal_note": "User 8 (James O'Connor, Ops, Warehouse Supervisor) reports orders@ shared mailbox disappeared from Outlook today. Account active, not locked or blocked. Mailbox 29.7% used, so quota isn't the cause. Device BL-DT-0108 is offline right now, last check-in 2026-10-09 13:03 UTC, no warnings. That may just mean he's outside his usual hours (06:00-14:00 CT). I have no tool to check shared mailbox permissions, so I can't confirm whether his access to orders@ was removed. Sent KB-011 steps (restart Outlook, add mailbox manually, test in OWA) and asked him to report back. If OWA says access denied, escalate to Tier 2 under KB-011/KB-006. Access needs to be re-granted with mailbox owner approval.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
